    "body": "RFC 9110 section [12.5.3. Accept-Encoding](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9110/#section-12.5.3) [says](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9110/#section-12.5.3-9):\n\n>  A server tests whether a content coding for a given representation is acceptable using these rules:\n>\n> 1. If no Accept-Encoding header field is in the request, any content coding is considered acceptable by the user agent.\n\nIt seems reasonable to assume that `accepts(req).encoding('anything')` should not return `false`, but `'anything'` as it should be accepted. Similarly, `accepts(req).encoding()` IMO should return `['*']`. This is already done for `Accept`/`.type()` (#20) and the readme hints that it's done for all headers (though, maybe I misinterpret this point):\n\nhttps://github.com/jshttp/accepts/blob/19db02a05c325e1814833c1b6fde58acdb5ba96a/index.js#L100-L103\n\nhttps://github.com/jshttp/accepts/blob/19db02a05c325e1814833c1b6fde58acdb5ba96a/README.md?plain=1#L18\n\nInterestingly, there is a test for this incorrect behaviour:\n\nhttps://github.com/jshttp/accepts/blob/19db02a05c325e1814833c1b6fde58acdb5ba96a/test/encoding.js#L17-L32\n\nThere is a similar paragraph in the older [RFC 7231](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7231/#section-5.3.4), but the even older RFC 2616 [says](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2616/#section-14.3) something slightly different, which may explain the current behaviour:\n\n> If no Accept-Encoding field is present in a request, the server MAY\n> assume that the client will accept any content coding. In this case,\n> if \"identity\" is one of the available content-codings, then the\n> server SHOULD use the \"identity\" content-coding, unless it has\n> additional information that a different content-coding is meaningful\n> to the client.\n>\n>    Note: If the request does not include an Accept-Encoding field,\n>    and if the \"identity\" content-coding is unavailable, then\n>    content-codings commonly understood by HTTP/1.0 clients (i.e.,\n>    \"gzip\" and \"compress\") are preferred;\n\nI don't see anything similar for `Accept-Charset` and it's [deprecated](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9110/#section-12.5.2-6.1). `Accept-Language` is handled by [`negotiator`](https://github.com/jshttp/negotiator/blob/14b0a7b88e7e7bb1cae38681195951bff29ca2fd/test/language.js#L86-L95).",
